author zichuanxu <zichuanxu28@gmail.com> 1790811344 +0900
committer zichuanxu <zichuanxu28@gmail.com> 1790811344 +0900

Registered controls staged and written; key-audit and block-L token-share macros; M1 table and neighbour cell

Controls (runs/stage5_controls, worlds 1000-1009, 23 runs, all implementation checks pass):
11 of 20 predictions hold, 6 fail (P-G3, P-T3, P-K2, P-Z2, and the validity conditions P-M3,
P-D2), 3 are not judged (P-M1, P-M2, P-D1). By the readings registered before the results:
D0full reads "execution" (repair gap 77.9 / 93.6 pp on definition items, access gain 0.0 /
+1.0 pp); the template moves definition items by at most 0.6 pp but costs 35.2 pp on all items
after a deletion; the oracle key keeps the refresh's Update but not its Stability; a refresh
without invalidation recovers 1.00 of the binding effect on definition items; the query-time
view matches the stored derivation on definition items, so design rule 5 becomes "compute
definition items at read time rather than store and bind them".

Also: the offline key audit as a stage with KeyAudit macros and tab_keyaudit (values equal the
decision log); block-L token shares (digests 99.1% of body text, rewritten bodies 0.9% of each
world, approximate tokens); M1 per-switch table prints undefined fits as dashes with a caveat
mark; the neighbour table's world-text cell shows T (+L) now that block L has run; control
captions say "registered after the main results were known" consistently; the M1 reading on
agreement against the new writer's accuracy; the exploratory-macro compile test decodes TeX
output with replacement.

